From 618e664336736cb6a89808f353247edfd5c73d0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:59:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Player information] Whether the EDID comes through a
 sound bar or AV receiver, and its sound formats

A sound bar, an AV receiver or a switch that passes HDMI on makes an EDID of its own for each of its inputs, so
what the PC reads there is what that device declares, not the TV's: the same LG C5 read through a TCL Q85H Pro
gives a Dolby Vision block of version 1 instead of 2, DTS and DTS-HD that the TV does not take, and FRL 40 Gb/s
instead of 48. Users compared those values with the TV's specification and took them for a fault, and nothing on
the system page of the player information said where they came from.

HDMI gives every source a physical address, which the sink writes into the HDMI VSDB of the EDID of each of its
inputs (HDMI 1.4b, 8.7): a PC on input 4 of the TV reads 4.0.0.0, one on input 2 of a sound bar that is on the
TV's input 2 reads 2.2.0.0. EdidHdmiPath.h reads that address and the audio data blocks from the raw EDID:
- how many devices are between the source and the display (0 for A.0.0.0, 1 for A.B.0.0...), unknown where the
  address says nothing (F.F.F.F, 0.0.0.0, a nibble after a 0) or where there is no HDMI VSDB (DisplayPort);
- the sound formats that matter for a film, by their short names: TrueHD, DD+, DTS-HD, DTS, AC-3, PCM N ch.

Checked on EDIDs of the C5 read both ways (4.0.0.0 without DTS; 2.2.0.0 with DTS and DTS-HD), and on the 584 TV,
receiver and projector EDIDs of the linuxhw database that the bridge's tests use: every one of the 27 AV
receivers reads as behind one device, 528 TVs as direct.

The system page of the player information has two rows more under what the display declares: Sound (the formats
of the EDID) and Connection ("Direct (4.0.0.0)", or "Via a sound bar or receiver (2.2.0.0)", the second saying
that the rows above are that device's). kodi.log says it once per EDID ([display-info] hdmi address ...; sound
formats declared ...). The pages of the player information for other skins are made again from Estuary's
(tools/hades-playerinfo/make-playerinfo.py).
