+++ b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
@@ -5695,3 +5695,23 @@ msgstr ""
 msgctxt "#54502"
 msgid "Lets the display switch to its HDR mode for HDR videos. On (the default): HDR10, HDR10+ and HLG videos go out as HDR, and the display shows them in its HDR mode. Off: the display stays in SDR, and those videos are converted to SDR, as for a display without HDR (see \"HDR to SDR: the display it is made for\"). Dolby Vision videos, and the videos that a setting sends as Dolby Vision, still go out as Dolby Vision while \"Native Dolby Vision output\" is on: to have them as SDR too, turn that off as well, or, for one video, choose \"As SDR (without HDR)\" for it while it plays, in \"Output of this video\" of the player information (the O key of a keyboard, Info on a remote, then OK on that button). To send only HLG videos as SDR, leave this on and use \"Play HDR videos as SDR\", below. Applies from the next video."
 msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades, system page of the player information, what the TV declares: the name of the row that says whether the EDID comes from the TV itself or through another device (its HDMI address follows the value)
+msgctxt "#54520"
+msgid "Connection"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades, system page of the player information, row "Connection": the PC is on an input of the TV itself (the HDMI address follows, as "(4.0.0.0)")
+msgctxt "#54521"
+msgid "Direct"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades, system page of the player information, row "Connection": the EDID comes through a sound bar, an AV receiver or a switch, so what the rows above say is what that device declares (the HDMI address follows, as "(2.2.0.0)"). One line of about 410 pixels with the address
+msgctxt "#54522"
+msgid "Via a sound bar or receiver"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades, system page of the player information, what the TV declares: the name of the row of the sound formats of its EDID (TrueHD, DD+, DTS-HD, DTS, AC-3, PCM and its channels)
+msgctxt "#54523"
+msgid "Sound"
+msgstr ""
